From b4fb1f026bae71a08a06a764ed0acf6c687f4d6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chimera <ctitus@umd.edu>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 10:24:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sys_status: request AUTOPILOT_VERSION via REQUEST_MESSAGE

PX4 v1.18 removed the legacy command shims from mavlink_receiver.cpp.
MAV_CMD_REQUEST_AUTOPILOT_CAPABILITIES (520) now falls through to the
default case, and the FCU answers MAV_RESULT_UNSUPPORTED (3).

MAVROS therefore never receives AUTOPILOT_VERSION from the autopilot.
The sys plugin retries five times and then gives up:

  [WARN]  CMD: Unexpected command 520, result 3
  [WARN]  VER: broadcast request timeout, retries left 4
  [ERROR] VER: command plugin service call failed!
  [WARN]  VER: your FCU don't support AUTOPILOT_VERSION,
          switched to default capabilities

The fallback capability set omits MAV_PROTOCOL_CAPABILITY_MISSION_INT,
so the waypoint plugin stays on the deprecated MISSION_ITEM protocol.

MAV_CMD_REQUEST_MESSAGE (512) is the generic replacement. PX4 v1.15,
v1.16, v1.17 and v1.18 all handle it in handle_message_command_long().

Verified on an EchoPilot AI running PX4 v1.18.0-beta1. The FCU answers
MAV_RESULT_ACCEPTED and sends AUTOPILOT_VERSION with capabilities
0x000000000004e8ff. The waypoint plugin then logs "Using MISSION_ITEM_INT".
---
 mavros/src/plugins/sys_status.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mavros/src/plugins/sys_status.cpp b/mavros/src/plugins/sys_status.cpp
index e36a96d..6d793d3 100644
--- a/mavros/src/plugins/sys_status.cpp
+++ b/mavros/src/plugins/sys_status.cpp
@@ -1311,9 +1311,13 @@ private:
 
       auto cmdrq = std::make_shared<mavros_msgs::srv::CommandLong::Request>();
       cmdrq->broadcast = do_broadcast;
-      cmdrq->command = enum_value(MAV_CMD::REQUEST_AUTOPILOT_CAPABILITIES);
+      // PX4 v1.18 dropped the legacy REQUEST_AUTOPILOT_CAPABILITIES (520) shim and
+      // answers it MAV_RESULT_UNSUPPORTED, so the FCU never emits AUTOPILOT_VERSION
+      // and MAVROS falls back to default capabilities. REQUEST_MESSAGE (512) is the
+      // generic replacement; PX4 v1.15 through v1.18 all handle it.
+      cmdrq->command = enum_value(MAV_CMD::REQUEST_MESSAGE);
       cmdrq->confirmation = false;
-      cmdrq->param1 = 1.0;
+      cmdrq->param1 = mavlink::standard::msg::AUTOPILOT_VERSION::MSG_ID;
 
       RCLCPP_DEBUG(
         lg, "VER: Sending %s request.",
